Dear Ahmad,

Thank you for the clear note. Good to hear the work is progressing. Answers
below.

1. Tools: Yes. Hosted APIs, local models and an AI coding assistant are all
fine, including in the live session, as long as they are documented as you
describe.

2. Pack completeness: The pack is complete as provided. Treat Volume III
and Drawing 03-C-114 as referenced but not supplied, and flag the gaps and
their impact. That is part of the exercise.

3. Addendum 3: Yes, it will be a PDF in the same format as Addenda 1 and 2,
shared at the start of the live session.

4. Prior Q&A: No written clarifications have been issued to other
candidates. Anything we share with you is shared on the same basis.

5. A5 programme: Your basis is fine. Use the latest addendum date as the
planning date, keep the consortium and external assumptions as editable
settings, and label them clearly.

6. Delivery: Your proposed single archive and formats work for us.

We look forward to receiving it by 17:00 Monday 5 October at the latest.

Best regards,
Hiring team for Hani Abdelhadi, Lamar Holding

On Thu, Oct 01, 2026 12:50 PM, Ahmad Atieh <ahmadtalalateya@gmail.com>
wrote:

> Dear Hiring Team,
>
> Thank you for accommodating my return. Work is progressing well, and I
> have a few confirmations and questions. Where I state an intended approach,
> I will proceed on that basis unless you advise otherwise.
>
> *Tools*
> I will use hosted model APIs (such as Claude) and/or local models on my
> own machine, together with an AI coding assistant, including during the
> session. All tools and model usage will be documented.
>
> *The Pack*
> Volume III: Volume III (Drawings) is referenced in the RFP, including
> Drawing 03-C-114, but was not included among the six PDFs received. I will
> therefore treat it as referenced but not supplied and flag any resulting
> gaps. Please confirm that the pack is complete as provided.
>
> Third addendum: I am assuming the addendum provided during the session
> will be a PDF, broadly in the same format as Addenda No. 1 and 2. Please
> let me know if it will be provided differently.
>
> Earlier questions: If any Q&A or clarifications have already been shared
> with other candidates, I would appreciate receiving them as well.
>
> *Planning Inputs for the Programme (A5)*
> Planning date: As programme dates are calculated backwards from the
> Proposal Due Date, I will use the latest addendum date as the planning
> date. Based on the current pack, this is 22 October 2026, and during the
> session I will update it to the date of the third addendum. Please advise
> if you prefer another basis.
>
> Bidder: The pack does not identify the bidder, but some requirements apply
> to each consortium member (for example, declarations and powers of
> attorney), so the plan needs a member count. Unless otherwise instructed, I
> will plan for an unnamed three-member consortium, with the name and number
> of members as editable settings. Bidder-specific facts not in the pack,
> such as references, certificates and financial standing, will be flagged
> for confirmation rather than assumed.
>
> External assumptions: Where the pack does not provide information such as
> Saudi public holidays, document-issuance durations, or bid-team roles, I
> will use reasonable external assumptions and clearly label them as editable
> assumptions with their basis.
>
> *Delivery*
> Formats: I plan to submit one archive containing:
>
>    - A1 and A5: CSV and JSON, with A1 also in Excel.
>    - A2: Markdown report with supporting CSV/JSON tables.
>    - A3: One-page PDF.
>    - A4: Repository including commit history, prompts, model-call log and
>    work log.
>
> The outputs can be rebuilt offline, so no API key is needed and none is
> included.
>
> Kind regards,
> Ahmad
>
>>

